// A GRACE'S DOT IS PUSHED BY THE FLAG ON THE STEM THAT IS DRAWN, not by the one a flat
// side model would have drawn.
//
// The augmentation dot of an unbeamed flagged note stands right of the FLAG whenever the flag's
// ink reaches the row the dot ended up on (lily/dot-column.cc:100-141). For a GRACE the flag
// hangs off a short stem, so the gate turns — and what turns it is the stem's LENGTH, which
// LilyPond shortens for a note above the middle line. Until session 315 Lily# measured that
// flag off a retired flat stem (3.5 x the font scale = 2.475 for every duration and every
// pitch), which pushed EVERY lifted dot and so got the first line below wrong by 0.5207.
//
// MEASURED on canonical LilyPond 2.26.0 (scratch/p315/gracedot-dump.ly dumps the NoteHead /
// Dots / Stem / Flag extents; each number is the dot's LEFT minus its own head's LEFT, and
// Lily#'s absolute `c` is LilyPond's `c'`):
//   g8.   ON A LINE, dot lifted, stem 2.80 (no shortening)   1.226585  <- the flag stays clear
//   f8.   IN A SPACE, dot not lifted, stem 2.80              1.226585
//   d'8.  ON A LINE, dot lifted, stem SHORTENED to 2.50      1.747274  <- the flag comes down
//   e'8.  IN A SPACE, stem 2.40                              1.226585
//   d'16. ON A LINE, stem 2.50                               1.747274
//   g16.  ON A LINE, stem 2.80                               1.747274  <- a 16th flag is 0.354
//                                                                         deeper, so it reaches
//                                                                         without the shortening
// where the head's own ink right is 0.917939 and one grace dot is 0.308646, and the flag's own
// right edge is 1.438627.
//
// The last measure is the BEAMED control: a beamed column draws no flag at all, so its lifted
// dot stays at the head's right whatever the stem does. It is also what keeps this book honest
// about who withholds the stem (SharedRenderer.BuildBeamedItemsSet).
octave absolute
time 4/4

part v { }

section A {
  v {
    grace { g8. } c'1 |
    grace { f8. } c'1 |
    grace { d'8. } c'1 |
    grace { e'8. } c'1 |
  }
}

section B {
  v {
    grace { d'16. } c'1 |
    grace { g16. } c'1 |
    grace { g16. g16 } c'1 |
  }
}

form main { ~A ~B }

score main { staff ~v }
